# Native iOS rules (Swift/Objective-C, Info.plist, entitlements, project.pbxproj)
# Generated from the threat library cards (threats/ios/*); each rule cites its card.
# Fields (tab-separated, "-" = empty):
#   rule_id threat_id severity type file_globs pattern message card flags [exclude]
# Severity: high/critical block the build by default; medium/low warn.
# Heuristic rules are kept one level below the card severity so they warn.
IOS-KC-001	ios-keychain-accessibility	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	kSecAttrAccessibleAlways	kSecAttrAccessibleAlways* is deprecated and readable while locked: use kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly	ios/keychain-accessibility.md	-
IOS-KC-002	ios-keychain-accessibility	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlock([^T]|$)	AfterFirstUnlock (without ThisDeviceOnly) is readable while locked and migrates in backups: use ...ThisDeviceOnly, and AfterFirstUnlock only for background needs	ios/keychain-accessibility.md	-
IOS-KC-003	ios-keychain-accessibility	low	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlocked([^T]|$)	WhenUnlocked items migrate to other devices via backup: prefer kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly for device-bound secrets	ios/keychain-accessibility.md	-
IOS-KC-004	ios-keychain-accessibility	medium	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;SecItemAdd\(;;!kSecAttrAccessible	Heuristic: Keychain item added without kSecAttrAccessible (default WhenUnlocked migrates via backup): set an explicit ThisDeviceOnly class	ios/keychain-accessibility.md	-
IOS-KS-001	ios-keychain-sharing	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	kSecAttrSynchronizable[^,;]*(true|kCFBooleanTrue|kSecAttrSynchronizableAny|@YES)	Keychain item syncs to iCloud Keychain and other devices: keep tokens and keys non-synchronizable	ios/storage/ios-keychain-sharing.md	-
IOS-KS-002	ios-keychain-sharing	medium	check	*.entitlements	plist;;keychain-access-groups;;\*	Wildcard keychain access group shares items with every app of the team: list exact groups	ios/storage/ios-keychain-sharing.md	-
IOS-DP-001	ios-weak-data-protection	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	NSFileProtectionNone|FileProtectionType\.none|\.noFileProtection|NSDataWritingFileProtectionNone	File written without Data Protection: use .completeFileProtection (NSFileProtectionComplete)	ios/storage/ios-weak-data-protection.md	-
IOS-DP-002	ios-weak-data-protection	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	[Cc]ompleteUntilFirstUserAuthentication|completeFileProtectionUntilFirstUserAuthentication	File stays readable while the device is locked: use .completeFileProtection for sensitive files	ios/storage/ios-weak-data-protection.md	-
IOS-DP-003	ios-weak-data-protection	low	check	*.entitlements	plist_absent;;com\.apple\.developer\.default-data-protection	No default Data Protection entitlement: add com.apple.developer.default-data-protection = NSFileProtectionComplete	ios/storage/ios-weak-data-protection.md	-
IOS-ST-001	ios-insecure-data-storage	medium	imatch	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(userdefaults|defaults)[^;]*(set|setobject|setvalue)[^;]*forkey:[[:space:]]*@?"[^"]*(token|password|passwd|secret|jwt|session|credential|cvv)	Heuristic: credential stored in UserDefaults (a plaintext plist that is backed up): store it in the Keychain	ios/storage/ios-insecure-data-storage.md	-
IOS-ST-002	ios-insecure-data-storage	medium	imatch	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	@AppStorage\("[^"]*(token|password|secret|jwt)	@AppStorage is UserDefaults: keep credentials in the Keychain	ios/storage/ios-insecure-data-storage.md	-
IOS-ST-003	ios-insecure-data-storage	medium	imatch	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(NSKeyedArchiver|PropertyListEncoder|JSONEncoder)[^;]*(token|password|secret|credential)	Heuristic: credential serialized to a file: keep it in the Keychain, or encrypt and use complete file protection	ios/storage/ios-insecure-data-storage.md	-
IOS-BK-001	ios-backup-icloud-exposure	medium	imatch	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(NSUbiquitousKeyValueStore|CKRecord)[^;]*(token|password|secret)	Credential synced through iCloud: never sync secrets; keep them in a non-synchronizable ThisDeviceOnly Keychain item	ios/storage/ios-backup-icloud-exposure.md	-
IOS-BK-002	ios-backup-icloud-exposure	low	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;\.documentDirectory|NSDocumentDirectory;;(write\(to:|\.write\(|writeToFile|createFile);;!isExcludedFromBackup|NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey	Heuristic: files in Documents are backed up: set isExcludedFromBackup for caches and sensitive files	ios/storage/ios-backup-icloud-exposure.md	-
IOS-SE-001	ios-secure-enclave-misuse	medium	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;SecKeyCreateRandomKey\(;;!kSecAttrTokenIDSecureEnclave	Private key generated outside the Secure Enclave: add kSecAttrTokenID = kSecAttrTokenIDSecureEnclave (P-256) with an access control	ios/storage/ios-secure-enclave-misuse.md	-
IOS-SE-002	ios-secure-enclave-misuse	low	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	P256\.(Signing|KeyAgreement)\.PrivateKey\(\)	CryptoKit key lives in app memory: use SecureEnclave.P256 keys for device-bound identity	ios/storage/ios-secure-enclave-misuse.md	-	SecureEnclave\.
IOS-LA-001	ios-localauthentication-misuse	medium	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;evaluatePolicy;;!SecAccessControl|kSecUseAuthenticationContext|kSecAccessControl	Heuristic: biometric result is used as a boolean gate (hookable): bind the secret to a Keychain item with SecAccessControl(.biometryCurrentSet)	ios/auth/ios-localauthentication-misuse.md	-
IOS-LA-002	ios-localauthentication-misuse	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	touchIDAuthenticationAllowableReuseDuration[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*[1-9]|LATouchIDAuthenticationMaximumAllowableReuseDuration	Biometric reuse window lets an earlier unlock authorize this action: set it to 0 for sensitive operations	ios/auth/ios-localauthentication-misuse.md	-
IOS-LA-003	ios-localauthentication-misuse	low	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	evaluatedPolicyDomainState	evaluatedPolicyDomainState is deprecated: use domainState / .biometryCurrentSet	ios/auth/ios-localauthentication-misuse.md	-
IOS-WV-001	ios-wkwebview-file-access	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(allowFileAccessFromFileURLs|allowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs)[^;]*(true|YES)|(true|YES)[^;]*(allowFileAccessFromFileURLs|allowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs)	Private WKWebView file-access flags let file:// pages read other files: remove them	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-file-access.md	-
IOS-WV-002	ios-wkwebview-file-access	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	allowingReadAccessTo(URL)?:[[:space:]]*(URL\(fileURLWithPath:[[:space:]]*("/"|NSHomeDirectory)|.*(documentDirectory|NSHomeDirectory|applicationSupportDirectory))	loadFileURL grants read access to a whole container directory: pass only the directory of the bundled page	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-file-access.md	-
IOS-WV-003	ios-wkwebview-message-handlers	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	\.add\([[:space:]]*[A-Za-z_.]+,[[:space:]]*name:|addScriptMessageHandler(WithReply)?[(:]	Heuristic: script message handler is reachable from every frame/origin: register it in a WKContentWorld and check message.frameInfo.securityOrigin	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-message-handlers.md	-	contentWorld
IOS-WV-004	ios-wkwebview-message-handlers	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	evaluateJavaScript\([[:space:]]*"[^"]*\\\(|evaluateJavaScript:[[:space:]]*\[NSString[[:space:]]+stringWithFormat	JavaScript is built by string interpolation (script injection): pass data with callAsyncJavaScript(arguments:) or JSON-encode it	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-message-handlers.md	-
IOS-WV-005	ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	UIWebView	UIWebView is deprecated, insecure and rejected by App Store review: migrate to WKWebView	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content.md	-
IOS-WV-006	incorrect-certificate-validation	critical	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;\.useCredential,[[:space:]]*URLCredential\([[:space:]]*trust:|NSURLSessionAuthChallengeUseCredential;;!SecTrustEvaluateWithError|SecTrustEvaluate\(|evaluateTrust|TrustKit|[Pp]inn|ServerTrustManager|SecTrustCopyCertificateChain|SecTrustGetCertificateAtIndex	Server trust is accepted without evaluation: call SecTrustEvaluateWithError (plus pinning if used) before .useCredential, otherwise .performDefaultHandling	shared/crypto/incorrect-certificate-validation.md	-
IOS-WV-007	ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content	medium	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsInWebContent;;<true/>	ATS is disabled for web content: remove NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsInWebContent and load https only	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content.md	-
IOS-WV-008	ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content	low	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;decidePolicyFor;;decisionHandler\(\.allow\);;!decisionHandler\(\.cancel\)	Heuristic: navigation delegate allows every navigation: allow-list scheme and host and cancel the rest	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-untrusted-content.md	-
IOS-ATS-001	attacker-in-the-middle	high	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSAllowsArbitraryLoads;;<true/>	App Transport Security is disabled: remove NSAllowsArbitraryLoads and use https (scoped NSExceptionDomains only if unavoidable)	shared/network/attacker-in-the-middle.md	-
IOS-ATS-002	attacker-in-the-middle	medium	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads|NSTemporaryExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads;;<true/>	ATS exception allows cleartext HTTP for a domain: move that domain to https	shared/network/attacker-in-the-middle.md	-
IOS-ATS-003	attacker-in-the-middle	medium	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSExceptionMinimumTLSVersion|NSTemporaryExceptionMinimumTLSVersion;;TLSv1\.[01]	ATS exception allows TLS 1.0/1.1: require TLS 1.2+	shared/network/attacker-in-the-middle.md	-
IOS-DL-001	ios-deep-link-abuse	low	check	Info.plist	plist;;CFBundleURLSchemes;;<string>	Custom URL scheme can be claimed by other apps: prefer Universal Links, use ASWebAuthenticationSession + PKCE for OAuth, and validate every parameter	ios/webview/ios-deep-link-abuse.md	-
IOS-DL-002	ios-deep-link-abuse	low	check	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	cooccur;;onOpenURL|openURLContexts|open[[:space:]]+url:[[:space:]]*URL|continue[[:space:]]+userActivity;;!\.host[[:space:]]*==|allowedHosts|[Aa]llow[Ll]ist|[Ww]hitelist|scheme[[:space:]]*==|switch[[:space:]]+(url|components)	Heuristic: URL handler shows no scheme/host validation: allow-list scheme, host and parameters before acting	ios/webview/ios-deep-link-abuse.md	-
IOS-EN-001	ios-entitlement-misconfig	high	check	*.entitlements	plist;;get-task-allow;;<true/>	get-task-allow lets debuggers attach: remove it from committed entitlements (Xcode sets it for debug signing only)	ios/integrity/ios-entitlement-misconfig.md	-
IOS-EN-002	ios-entitlement-misconfig	low	check	*.entitlements	plist;;aps-environment;;development	aps-environment is development: confirm distribution exports switch it to production	ios/integrity/ios-entitlement-misconfig.md	-
IOS-EN-003	ios-entitlement-misconfig	medium	check	*.entitlements	plist;;com\.apple\.developer\.associated-domains;;applinks:\*	Wildcard associated domain trusts every subdomain (subdomain takeover risk): list exact hosts	ios/integrity/ios-entitlement-misconfig.md	-
IOS-RE-001	ios-reverse-engineering	medium	check	*.pbxproj	within;;/\* Release \*/ = \{;;STRIP_INSTALLED_PRODUCT = NO|ENABLE_TESTABILITY = YES|SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = "-Onone"|GCC_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = 0	Release configuration keeps symbols / testability / no optimization: restore the Release defaults	ios/integrity/ios-reverse-engineering.md	-
IOS-RE-002	debug-mode-in-production	high	check	*.pbxproj	within;;/\* Release \*/ = \{;;"DEBUG=1"|DEBUG=1;|SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = "?[^;]*DEBUG	DEBUG is defined in the Release configuration, so #if DEBUG code ships: remove it from Release	shared/config-infra/debug-mode-in-production.md	-
IOS-LOG-001	sensitive-data-in-logs	high	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(print|NSLog|os_log|debugPrint|[Ll]ogger\.[a-z]+)\(.*(\\\(|,[[:space:]]*|\+[[:space:]]*)[A-Za-z_.]*([Pp]assword|[Pp]asswd|[Tt]oken|[Ss]ecret|[Jj]wt|JWT|[Cc]vv|CVV|[Oo]tp[^a-z]|OTP|PASSWORD|TOKEN|SECRET)	Credential written to the device log: remove it, or log with privacy: .private / a redacted value	shared/data-privacy/sensitive-data-in-logs.md	-	[dD]eviceToken|privacy:[[:space:]]*\.private|\{private\}
IOS-PN-001	ios-push-apns-security	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	(print|NSLog|os_log|[Ll]ogger\.[a-z]+)\(.*[dD]eviceToken	APNs device token written to the log: do not log it	ios/auth/ios-push-apns-security.md	-	privacy:[[:space:]]*\.private|\{private\}
IOS-PB-001	ios-data-leakage-surfaces	medium	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	UIPasteboard\.general[^;]*(\.string[[:space:]]*=|setString|setItems|\.items[[:space:]]*=)|\[UIPasteboard generalPasteboard\][[:space:]]*setString	Data copied to the general pasteboard is visible to other apps and Universal Clipboard: use setItems with .localOnly and .expirationDate	ios/storage/ios-data-leakage-surfaces.md	-	localOnly|expirationDate
IOS-PB-002	ios-data-leakage-surfaces	low	match	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	UIScreen\.main\.isCaptured	UIScreen.isCaptured is deprecated: use the scene sceneCaptureState and redact sensitive content	ios/storage/ios-data-leakage-surfaces.md	-
IOS-AG-001	ios-app-group-leakage	medium	imatch	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h	userdefaults\(suitename:[^)]*\)[^;]*set[^;]*forkey:[[:space:]]*"[^"]*(token|password|secret)	Credential stored in shared App Group defaults (readable by every app in the group): use a Keychain item with an explicit access group	ios/webview/ios-app-group-leakage.md	-
IOS-AX-001	ios-app-extension-abuse	medium	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSExtensionActivationRule;;TRUEPREDICATE	Extension activates for any content (TRUEPREDICATE): declare the exact supported types	ios/webview/ios-app-extension-abuse.md	-
IOS-PM-001	ios-excessive-permissions	low	check	Info.plist	plist;;NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription|NSLocationAlwaysUsageDescription;;.	App asks for Always location: use When-In-Use unless background location is essential	ios/auth/ios-excessive-permissions.md	-
IOS-PM-002	ios-excessive-permissions	medium	check	Info.plist	plist;;NS[A-Za-z]+UsageDescription;;^(<string>[[:space:]]*</string>|<string/>|<string>(TODO|todo|TBD|Description|Usage description)</string>)$	Permission prompt has an empty or placeholder purpose string: explain the specific use (also an App Store rejection reason)	ios/auth/ios-excessive-permissions.md	-
IOS-SIGN-001	ios-enterprise-cert-abuse	low	file	*.mobileprovision	-	Provisioning profile is committed: manage profiles with fastlane match / CI secrets	ios/integrity/ios-enterprise-cert-abuse.md	gitignored-ok
IOS-INT-001	ios-app-tampering-repackaging	low	tree-absent	*.swift;*.m;*.mm;*.h;Podfile;*.dart;*.js;*.ts;*.tsx;pubspec.yaml;package.json	DCAppAttestService|DCDevice|IOSSecuritySuite|PT_DENY_ATTACH|/Applications/Cydia\.app|freerasp|JailMonkey|jail-monkey|flutter_jailbreak_detection|safe_device|Talsec|app_attest|AppAttest	No App Attest / integrity or jailbreak signal found: use App Attest with server-side verification for sensitive actions	ios/integrity/ios-app-tampering-repackaging.md	-
